I found a Mines 1 bones full of so many goodies I
had to retreat from the Mines to get better prepared
to use it. Giving up the protection racket as
unavailable, Wizard Grabby did some altar sitting on
DLVL 4 to build up stats and score MagicBane, and
intended to go clean out Sokoban with his pet large
cat Purrball, Grabby now at XL6 and AC -3.

Ugly ways to die:

Throw your cat a chameleon corpse, hoping for a
more buff pet, end up with a pet floating eye that
doesn't follow when you leash it, leave pet behind,
do Sokoban unaided.

Get burdened in Sokoban, and drop all the stuff you
don't need right now, stupidly on the same level
where you're playing (second sokoban).

Have a kobold shaman use your stash to nail you with
your own potion, zap you with your own wand, and read
one of your scrolls of earth, dropping a boulder on
your head, and incidentally building an "I" shaped
clot of boulders in a doorway you need in order to
get back to the rest of the mine.

Leave the kobold shaman dead, but the rest that
problem unsolved, since you have a pick-axe but
don't need the luck hit until after top level
Sokoban, and thus leave no fast way of retreat, find
the door to the room with the up-stairs open
_anyway_ (somebody on Team Monsters broke it), and
lots of monsters in there.

Die to a flight of woodland elves, ignoring such
resources as

  a ring of conflict, unworn
  an (unIDed) amulet of life saving, unworn
  a ring of protection +1, unworn
  the chance to run back down the newly paved
    hallway to rest up between kills
  two wands of sleep

Of course, the latter is what really got me, as I
zapped one wand of sleep at a woodland elf standing
in the door, at a careful 45 degree angle, and
demonstrated the truism that sometimes ray attacks
bounce straight back at the user anyway, even if the
shot should ricochet away.

YASD, oh, my that was stupid^3, but may I say
"AAAAAARGH" anyway?

